# Icons

Falcon uses the Hala icon set from the HALA DNA Figma file (Icons page). Draw icons through `icons/api.js` on web, which reads `vendor/hala-icons.js`. Do not paste SVG paths, use another icon set, or use emoji.

```js
import { icon } from "./icons/api.js";

button.append(icon("transfers"));
row.append(icon("search", { size: "inline" }));
tile.append(icon("cards", { tone: "default" }));
```

## Drawing

- Hala icons are filled shapes on a 16 grid in two tones: icon/primary and icon/secondary. No strokes.
- Color is `currentColor`. Set it with a text or status token (`--text-primary`, `--text-tertiary`, `--brand-600`, `--status-danger`). No gradient or one-off color.
- Both tones use `currentColor` unless you pass `tone: "default"` (text/primary + text/tertiary) or `tone: "secondary"` (text/secondary + text/tertiary). The secondary tone reads `--icon-secondary`.
- Sizes are `inline` 16, `default` 20, `nav` 22, and `feature` 28. One size per row.
- Names come from the Falcon catalog in `icons/api.js`: `transfers`, `search`, `cards`. The same name is used on Web, Android, and iOS.
- An icon-only control has a tooltip and an accessible name.
- In RTL, `data-mirror` icons flip. Search, check, bell, card, clock, and charts do not.

## Lucide fallbacks

Eight Falcon names have no Hala match and stay on Lucide 0.453.0 (ISC), as in the Figma Lucide category: `account`, `wallet`, `savings`, `trend-up`, `trend-down`, `delivery`, `email`, `phone`. The spinner (`loader-circle`) and `linkedin` also stay on Lucide. These draw at `var(--icon-stroke)` (1.7), and active navigation uses `var(--icon-stroke-active)` (2.2).

## Adding an icon

1. Pick it from the HALA DNA Icons page. Ask design if no Hala icon fits.
2. Export its paths and checksum into `icons/source/` (a new `batch-N.json` and a line in `sums.json`).
3. Map the Falcon name in `catalog` in `icons/build.mjs`, then run `npm run build:icons`. The build fails if a path does not match Figma.

## React

When a component is React, wrap `icon()` once in a `HalaIcon` component with `name`, `size`, and `tone` props. Do not add `lucide-react` for Hala icons.
